{
  "topic": "The physics of Christmas Eve",
  "language": "en",
  "format": "long",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "Could SANTA Deliver Every Present in ONE Night? 🎅",
  "hook": "Every December twenty-fourth, Santa has to deliver presents all over the world in a single night.",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_hook",
      "narration": "Every December twenty-fourth, Santa has to deliver presents all over the world in a single night.",
      "on_screen_text": "A single night",
      "highlight_words": [
        "night"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_speed",
      "narration": "Is it possible? Let's do the math with real physics, no magic… at least at first.",
      "on_screen_text": "Let's do the math",
      "highlight_words": [
        "math"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_gifts",
      "narration": "I'm Leo, and today we figure out what it would take. Spoiler: the sleigh would be the fastest machine in history.",
      "on_screen_text": "The fastest machine",
      "highlight_words": [
        "fastest"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_kids",
      "narration": "First, how many children are there? Nearly two billion people in the world are under fifteen.",
      "on_screen_text": "≈ 2 billion kids",
      "highlight_words": [
        "kids"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "How many kids"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_kids",
      "narration": "Let's assume about three kids per home on average. That's hundreds of millions of homes in one night.",
      "on_screen_text": "Hundreds of millions of homes",
      "highlight_words": [
        "homes"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_zones",
      "narration": "But Santa has a trick: time zones. Midnight doesn't arrive everywhere at once.",
      "on_screen_text": "The time-zone trick",
      "highlight_words": [
        "time-zone"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "Help from the clock"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_zones",
      "narration": "If he starts in the Pacific islands, where Christmas comes first, and travels west following the night, he gets more than thirty hours.",
      "on_screen_text": "Over 30 hours",
      "highlight_words": [
        "30"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_zones",
      "narration": "The first places to reach Christmas are Pacific islands like Kiribati, fourteen hours ahead of world time.",
      "on_screen_text": "Kiribati goes first",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Kiribati"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_zones",
      "narration": "In some countries presents arrive on other days, like January sixth with the Three Kings, and that helps too.",
      "on_screen_text": "Other gift days",
      "highlight_words": [
        "days"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "mit_spin",
      "narration": "It's like running alongside the night as Earth turns, so it stays the middle of the night wherever he is.",
      "on_screen_text": "Racing the night",
      "highlight_words": [
        "night"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_speed",
      "narration": "Even so, the numbers are wild: he'd have to visit about six thousand homes per second.",
      "on_screen_text": "6,000 homes per second",
      "highlight_words": [
        "6,000"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "Sleigh speed"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_speed",
      "narration": "If homes were a kilometer apart, the sleigh would travel thousands of kilometers per second.",
      "on_screen_text": "Thousands of km per second",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Thousands"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_speed",
      "narration": "At each house he'd have just a tiny fraction of a second to come down, leave the presents and get back to the sleigh.",
      "on_screen_text": "A fraction of a second",
      "highlight_words": [
        "fraction"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "coh_orbit",
      "narration": "For comparison: a rocket in orbit goes about eight kilometers per second. The sleigh would be hundreds of times faster.",
      "on_screen_text": "Faster than a rocket",
      "highlight_words": [
        "rocket"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "coh_orbit",
      "narration": "Not even the fastest space probes we've ever built come close to that speed.",
      "on_screen_text": "Faster than any probe",
      "highlight_words": [
        "probe"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_burn",
      "narration": "And here's the problem. At that speed, the air in front of the sleigh would be squeezed and heated enormously.",
      "on_screen_text": "The air heats up",
      "highlight_words": [
        "heats"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The air problem"
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_burn",
      "narration": "The same thing that happens to a shooting star: it would glow like a meteor streaking across the sky.",
      "on_screen_text": "Like a shooting star",
      "highlight_words": [
        "shooting"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_burn",
      "narration": "On top of that, the reindeer would feel enormous forces every time they braked and sped up between houses.",
      "on_screen_text": "Brutal braking",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Brutal"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_gifts",
      "narration": "And the load would be gigantic. If each present weighed just half a kilo, it would add up to hundreds of thousands of tons.",
      "on_screen_text": "A gigantic load",
      "highlight_words": [
        "gigantic"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s20",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_gifts",
      "narration": "More than many cargo ships put together, pulled by just a few reindeer.",
      "on_screen_text": "More than a ship",
      "highlight_words": [
        "ship"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_gifts",
      "narration": "And he'd have to go down chimneys that many homes don't even have.",
      "on_screen_text": "Homes without chimneys",
      "highlight_words": [
        "chimneys"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_hook",
      "narration": "So with ordinary physics, it's impossible. That's why Christmas needs a little magic.",
      "on_screen_text": "It takes magic",
      "highlight_words": [
        "magic"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "So how does he do it?"
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_hook",
      "narration": "Or, as many people say, Santa's helpers are in every home in the world.",
      "on_screen_text": "Lots of helpers",
      "highlight_words": [
        "helpers"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_radar",
      "narration": "Surprise: there's a military agency that tracks him every year. Since 1955, NORAD has shared where the sleigh is on Christmas Eve.",
      "on_screen_text": "NORAD tracks him",
      "highlight_words": [
        "NORAD"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s25",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_radar",
      "narration": "It all began with a misprinted phone number in an ad. Kids called, and the officers decided to play along.",
      "on_screen_text": "It began with a mistake",
      "highlight_words": [
        "mistake"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s26",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_kids",
      "narration": "Today millions of families follow the trip online as night sweeps around the planet.",
      "on_screen_text": "Millions follow along",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Millions"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_kids",
      "narration": "And don't forget the letters: millions of kids write each year, and in several countries the post office has special addresses to answer them.",
      "on_screen_text": "Millions of letters",
      "highlight_words": [
        "letters"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_kids",
      "narration": "Not every family celebrates Christmas, but even so, the list would be enormous.",
      "on_screen_text": "An enormous list",
      "highlight_words": [
        "enormous"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s29",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_hook",
      "narration": "So next Christmas Eve, look up: if you see a shooting star, maybe it isn't dust, or maybe it is.",
      "on_screen_text": "Look up",
      "highlight_words": [
        "up"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_hook",
      "narration": "Real reindeer exist and live in the cold north, though of course none of them can fly.",
      "on_screen_text": "Real reindeer",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Real"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s31",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "nav_outro",
      "narration": "What other holiday question should we answer with science? Tell me in the comments. Merry Christmas!",
      "on_screen_text": "Merry Christmas!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Christmas!"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    }
  ],
  "description": "We do the math with physics: how many children, how many hours thanks to time zones, how fast the sleigh would go and what would happen to the air. A festive thought experiment. Original 3D animation; sizes and distances are not to scale.",
